{"text": "I found that `remap` already uses an internal registry for cycles and shared references. I’ll expose caching controls, forward them through `research`, and fix the zero-split case to return a list of the source’s values.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_QbQUrUi3FgbqJrwem0PQIGdz", "name": "repo__shell", "arguments": {"command": "python - <<'PY'\np='boltons/iterutils.py'\ns=open(p).read().replace('            yield [src]\\n', '            yield list(src)\\n', 1)\ns=s.replace('def remap(root, visit=default_visit, enter=default_enter, exit=default_exit,\\n          **kwargs):', 'def remap(root, visit=default_visit, enter=default_enter, exit=default_exit,\\n          cache=True, **kwargs):')\ns=s.replace('        reraise_visit (bool): A pragmatic convenience', '''        cache (bool or dict): Cache traversed objects by identity, so shared\n            references are traversed only once (the default). A dictionary\n            mapping object IDs to remapped objects may be supplied to share\n            the cache across calls. Keep the source objects alive while\n            reusing such a cache. Pass ``False`` to traverse shared objects\n            at each path; references to objects currently being traversed\n            are still tracked to prevent infinite loops. ``None`` uses a\n            fresh cache, like ``True``.\n        reraise_visit (bool): A pragmatic convenience''')\ns=s.replace('    path, registry, stack = (), {}, [(None, root)]', '''    registry = {} if cache is True or cache is False or cache is None else cache\n    if id(root) in registry:\n        return registry[id(root)]\n    path, stack = (), [(None, root)]''')\ns=s.replace('            registry[id_value] = value\\n            if not new_items_stack:', '''            if cache is False:\n                # Only active ancestors are needed for cycle detection.\n                del registry[id_value]\n            else:\n                registry[id_value] = value\n            if not new_items_stack:''')\ns=s.replace('def research(root, query=lambda p, k, v: True, reraise=False, enter=default_enter):', 'def research(root, query=lambda p, k, v: True, reraise=False, enter=default_enter,\\n             cache=True):')\ns=s.replace('          or to simply drop the result that caused the error.\\n', '''          or to simply drop the result that caused the error.\n       cache (bool or dict): Passed through to :func:`remap`. Defaults to\n          caching traversed objects. Pass ``False`` to search shared objects\n          at every path, while still avoiding circular traversal.\n''')\ns=s.replace('    remap(root, enter=_enter)', '    remap(root, enter=_enter, cache=cache)')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\npython -m pytest tests/test_iterutils.py -q", "timeout_s": 120}}], "usage": {"input_tokens": 3, "cache_read_tokens": 2284, "cache_write_tokens": 8006, "output_tokens": 970, "reasoning_tokens": 309, "source": "provider", "prompt_tokens": 10293, "completion_tokens": 970}, "model": "openai/gpt-6.1-sol", "finish": "tool_calls", "raw_message": {"reasoning_details": [{"type": "reasoning.encrypted", "data": "gAAAAABq1WUk4Qv2mQOv0Lcpb3dxSSQKXvl9nXe30Ko3kLieET7IREtm2pc0004pTzMoDFXoSG7pnhrMPPdirX3dbbuQYBWzUCg17l1kl8ywuOXdACqNCZHIbtuvtQGg6d58XklVAgSSc2_hAiZrWfQxeB7icl2CO-0BsXiNN4pR8FxtDITSkFoBupdGrks00JCiM5xw11ek8uIQPEcpvPp3Bjj2Ug4DlH-9Zvt9Z8PLql56jMpqw6fIRae0mjRG5iW1Q4c5nOOTf76HMYb2eDxVDvgW_Cd_ObbebNpbMxAiIdGIxVVKSiJ4MB5w2ATXOJ54wZodoZBJhRoMiRPVkTtwtKxgt0dYj428LABrb5Q9lR5TYC8qtcOy97sia-3kT0qDI0yxULEE076RIoC8C389NzRQKz0zUVOIicDZMugwgUbk_JCWRl6cyvo0Y9plTSjw1GBMWI8fN5TOYawslA8w66ySfKW9ZdUcT1K86BemjmUt2V8_VVyc2_LURTLp_CWno_fjd7A8uV_hzzK644dBXIKWFCPYdGc7g6EJG90yqjoeKE1UnMB6FFaOI234ammUokWmFyLDOO7FORbwe2Atxp0sYX2-cltKvdfD1g9SRV9BAqxUJSu0PIO_rEtPawldDrqpQ2Jy75YBN5PCqB23_MTrF_WCu0u41onJUJazOL_6CTA1srZfMOeYIwXuq8i7HcBDxieV-XSabVm9MXlLgDyj-j2Wpr97D1jUPrWX2lTRy4JeIxz9iXWmx6NPC3s34XQoXi8_bwP48TLOeyI18IGIJkY1_dU6DZYSUrBZig9oo1lutQG1WN39Q4HbTHxBct7koO-Nvay7501DWoQhJ0X0MJspS6gOKifHk2CVC-iaqi1